---
# Root C-core style: LLVM-based, normalised to what machines need:
#
# IndentWidth: 4 (whole-tree retune 2026-10-24: user-requested; replaces the
# earlier 2-space C-core style from issue #77).
# ColumnLimit: 150 — long enough that the tree's hand-shaped signature wraps
# and single-line macro bodies survive, but long lines are now wrapped at
# 150 rather than never re-wrapped.
# - AllowShort*: keeps the tree's unbraced single-line `if (x) y;` bodies.
# - SortIncludes: LLVM default (sorting on) — includes are re-sorted.
# - AlignTrailingComments: false and the AlignConsecutive* LLVM defaults
#   (all off) keep edits local: realigning one line must not ripple into
#   neighbours.
#
# C++ frontends keep their own configs: frontends/fcitx5/.clang-format and
# frontends/tsf/.clang-format (4-space, public: unindented, ColumnLimit 150).
# Vendored and generated trees are excluded via .clang-format-ignore.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
Language: Cpp
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 150
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: AllIfsAndElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: All
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
AllowShortEnumsOnASingleLine: true
ReflowComments: true
AlignTrailingComments: false
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Right
